644 - O God, Whose Will Is Life and Good
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 644
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[C7/E]O God, [F]whose will is [C7/Bb]life [Bb]and good
[F/C]For all [C7/Bb]of mortal [F/A]breath:
[Gm]Unite [F]in bonds [Dm]of [C7/E]servanthood
[C]All those who strive with death.

Verse 2:
[C7/E]Make strong [F]their hands and [C7/Bb]hearts [Bb]and wills
[F/C]To drive [C7/Bb]disease [F/A]afar,
[Gm]To [F]strive against [Dm]the [C7/E]body's [F/C]ills
[C]And wage Your healing war.

Verse 3:
[C7/E]By healing [F]of the [C7/Bb]sick [Bb]and blind,
[F/C]Christ's mercy [C7/Bb]they [F/A]proclaim,
[Gm]Make [F]known the great [Dm]physician's [F/C]mind,
[C]Affirm the Savior's name.

Verse 4:
[C7/E]Before [F]them set Your [C7/Bb]gracious [Bb/D]will,
[F/C]That they, [C7/Bb]with heart [F/A]and soul,
[Gm]To [F]You may consecrate their skill
[C]And make the sufferer whole.
